{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 09fbc3e4: fix all three in head C. Each is inside 00c50371.\n\n1. The `self` member. Keep `row.self` as the whole element. It is the readable form for the common case, a list of scalars, and the settled vocabulary uses it. Add one named helper that reads any member of a record element by name, `self` included. The helper is a function that the package exports, not a method on the record, so it cannot collide with a member name. The type of `row.self` on a record element is the whole element, also when the record has a member named `self`, so that the type and the runtime agree. The writing guide gets one sentence: use the helper for a member named `self`. Send me the signature in your next act. It does not wait for a reply unless I object.\n\n2. Rule references. Accepted: add `ruleReferences` to derive/rule, on the existing pinned JSONata parser and checked AST. Conditions:\n- It returns plain data, the direct field and value references of one rule source. It exports no AST and evaluates nothing.\n- A source that `admit` refuses gets the same refusal from the helper.\n- Admission, digests and pins do not change. The helper only reads.\n- The author package's `findings` uses it and drops the regex scan over rule text.\nderive is a published package, so the helper joins its public surface and its export witness in this head.\n\n3. Dotted indices. Correct the local boundary and assert the complete offending form. No new surface.\n\nTests: one case for each bug, three in all. For bug 2, the case is your quoted-text example: the expression reads no field and compiles with no finding. Add no other case.\n\nOrder: run the frozen compile-refusal control at 9f9dacf5 when the slot is free, then repair, then the affected focused owners, then the one final gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}